<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39555" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pulvĕrŭlentus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		id.. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>full of dust</i>, <i>dusty</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">via,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Att. 5, 14, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aestas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 1, 66</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">femina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					3, 14</span></i>
			 (4, 13), 7: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amnis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 3, 6, 96</span></i>
			; hence, also: Ceres, <i>covered with dust</i>
			in summer, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5, 742</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agmina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 4, 154</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>attended with
			labor</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praemia militiae,</span>”
				i. e. <i>toilsome</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 1, 15, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virtus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Vit. Beat. 7, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
